<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
        <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
        <AnalysisLevel>latest</AnalysisLevel>
        <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
        <EnforceExtendedAnalyzerRules>true</EnforceExtendedAnalyzerRules>
        <RunAnalyzersDuringBuild>true</RunAnalyzersDuringBuild>
        <RunAnalyzersDuringLiveAnalysis>true</RunAnalyzersDuringLiveAnalysis>
        <CodeAnalysisTreatWarningsAsErrors>true</CodeAnalysisTreatWarningsAsErrors>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <PropertyGroup>
        <!--
          Deterministic, source-linked release artifacts. ContinuousIntegrationBuild is unconditional
          rather than gated on a CI variable: eng/verify-reproducible-package.sh builds the same commit
          in two different directories and requires byte-identical packages, which only holds when
          source paths are normalised everywhere, and eng/verify-package.sh audits these properties and
          rejects a conditional declaration because its effective value cannot be read from the file.
        -->
        <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
        <ContinuousIntegrationBuild>true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
        <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
        <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
        <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
        <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <PropertyGroup>
        <PackageId>FriendlyEnvars</PackageId>
        <VersionPrefix>2.0.0</VersionPrefix>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>
## Intentional breaking changes in 2.0.0

- Exceptions are sealed and structured. EnvarsException is sealed and now carries FailureKind plus the
  environment-variable name, options type and name, property, target type, culture, binder type and the
  cause's type name. Library-generated failures never include the value, the cause's message or an inner
  exception, so a leaked log cannot disclose a secret. OperationCanceledException is propagated
  unchanged rather than wrapped.
- The two options-blocking configuration methods are removed with no replacement. IOptions,
  IOptionsSnapshot, IOptionsMonitor and IOptionsFactory all resolve normally.
- Property shapes and environment-variable names are validated eagerly, while BindEnvars runs, instead
  of lazily at options creation. A getter-only, static, indexed or non-public-setter property, or a name
  that is empty, whitespace only, contains '=' or contains a control character, now fails at
  registration even when the variable is absent.
- Registering FriendlyEnvars twice for the same options type and name throws InvalidOperationException.
- Values are captured once, while BindEnvars runs, and every options instance is built from that
  snapshot. Changing a variable afterwards no longer affects anything, including IOptionsSnapshot and
  IOptionsMonitor.
- Enum text follows an explicit grammar instead of Enum.Parse. Three differences from 1.1.0 are
  deliberate: a non-flags enum rejects the numeric "-1" even when a member such as All = -1 is declared;
  a non-flags enum rejects "Read,Write" even when ReadWrite = 3 is declared; and a flags enum rejects
  negative numeric text while still accepting the corresponding declared member name. Names that differ
  only by case are resolved deterministically, and a value whose bit pattern contains bits no declared
  member defines is rejected.
- BindEnvars&lt;T&gt; declares [DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicProperties)]
  on T, so trimmed applications preserve the properties reflection needs.
- The configured culture is cloned and frozen when it is captured. A binder that mutates the culture it
  is given now throws instead of silently changing how later values parse.

## Not new in 2.0

- Empty environment variables ("") have been passed to the binder rather than treated as unset since
  1.1.0. String properties become empty and non-string properties fail to convert. This is listed here
  only because it is often mistaken for a 2.0 change.

## Other changes

- XML documentation is generated and packaged.
- Lambdas that capture no state are marked static, reducing allocations.
- New package icon.
        </PackageReleaseNotes>
        <Authors>Lukasz Lepecki</Authors>
        <Description>Simplify your .NET configuration. FriendlyEnvars maps environment variables directly to strongly-typed options classes - no JSON files, no complex setup. Just define your settings class and you're done. Fully compatible with IOptions, naturally integrates with existing codebase.</Description>
        <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
        <PackageTags>configuration;options;environment-variables</PackageTags>
        <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Lukasz Lepecki</Copyright>
        <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/llepecki/friendly-envars</PackageProjectUrl>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/llepecki/friendly-envars</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <PackageIcon>icon-v2.png</PackageIcon>
        <GeneratePackageOnBuild>false</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
        <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>
        <PackageValidationBaselineVersion>1.1.0</PackageValidationBaselineVersion>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
            <_Parameter1>FriendlyEnvars.Tests</_Parameter1>
        </AssemblyAttribute>
    </ItemGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <ApiCompatSuppressionFile Include="CompatibilitySuppressions.xml" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
        <None Include="..\..\resources\icon-v2.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    </ItemGroup>
